{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>answered</b> — There are many words in the Chaldean language whose meaning is according to the sense of the context, and according to the reason of <i>azda</i> [certainty], like <b>קיימא</b> [established] and it is true, and the meaning is: this word shall be established. But <b>the dream and its interpretation you shall not make known to me</b> — you are liable to death. And Yefet said: <b>you shall be made pieces, pieces</b>. And he said: for <b>like it</b> is compared <b>the king of Samaria</b>, cut off, and thus <b>and I likened your mother</b>, as if he said: pieces, pieces you shall make with the sword. And the word <b>נולי</b> means ruins and desolation and waste. And R. Yeshuah said: like <b>דומן</b> [your likeness]."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes several Aramaic/Hebrew lexical forms; <b>נולי</b> and <b>דומן</b> are transliterated as Ibn Ezra cites them. 'R. Yeshuah' likely refers to R. Yeshuah ben Yehuda, a 10th-century Karaite exegete, as does Yefet; resolved by inference from Ibn Ezra's typical citation patterns."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:12.100679843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}